Not sure how you are generating your predictions but the lambda from a ZIP model gives you the mean abundance (N) for sites that have the species present.  So if you want a mean abundance across all sites (including the zeros), you need to use N = lambda*(1-psi) where psi is the zero-inflation parameter.  This is pointed out in the help file for pcount.

